      "message": "right, so we want to allow the \"admin\" on the admin domain to be the cloud admin.\n\nbut we don\u0027t want the \"domain admin\" to be able to be a \"cloud admin\"\n\nThe change we made to https://review.openstack.org/#/c/411563/9/keystone/models/token_model.py fixes that. Because if a \"domain admin\" requested a domain scoped token, it would automatically evaluate the \"is_admin_project:True\" to true !!\n\nThis is not necessary for domain scoped tokens",
